  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nAutumnal weather is expected through at least Tuesday/Tuesday\nevening as high pressure maintains influence over the region.\nTemperatures will be near to slightly below normal over the next\nseveral days with highs in the 60s and lower 70s and lows in the\n40s and 50s each day. By late Tuesday into Wednesday, low\npressure will drift into the Midwest with a cold front to the\nwest of the local area. Depending on the placement of the front,\nscattered showers may return to the area as early as Tuesday\nnight/early Wednesday, but it's possible that most of the area\nstays dry until Thursday or Friday when an upper trough moves\neast across the local area. At this point, impactful weather is\nnot expected with this system.",
